# K03 NS-ROLES-2 REQUIRED POSITIVE, red until its dependency is built (Codex K03-NS2-COVERAGE-20261007-21;
# steps/defects.md#reference-field-consumers).
# `b: tick` in Host's body binds b to tick's whole occurrence, as at the root and in a method (NS-ROLES-1b); Host's
# `got: b(5)` calls tick through b when Host runs.  Today a named body holds no binding to a callable: "a reference
# binding to a callable in a named Structure is not built yet" (the limit row unit_ns2_bind_callable_limit_refused).
# Exit 7; 81 if got is not tick's 6.
fn: tick (int: n) int
    return: n + 1
end: tick
Host:
    int: got 0
    b: tick
    got: b(5)
end: Host
fn: m () int
    Host()
    if: Host\got != 6
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
